"""Clap Counter preview pages; source for generated product/privacy/support HTML."""
def build(page):
    page('/clap-counter/', 'Clap Counter — Sound Counting for Android', 'Count claps, watch a live sound graph, and save sessions locally. Clap Counter for Android is in development.', '<style>\n.cc{--paper:#f9f7ef;--ink:#162d28;background:var(--paper);color:var(--ink);margin:24px 0;padding:clamp(22px,5vw,64px);border-radius:24px}.cc h1,.cc h2,.cc h3,.cc p,.cc li,.cc a{color:var(--ink)}.cc h1::first-line{color:var(--ink)}.cc .hero{padding:0}.cc h1{font-size:clamp(42px,6vw,78px);line-height:1.04;letter-spacing:-.045em;margin:22px 0}.cc h2{font-size:clamp(26px,3vw,38px);line-height:1.2}.cc p,.cc li{font-size:17px;line-height:1.7;max-width:65ch}.cc .eyebrow{font-size:12px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase}.cc .hero{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.2fr .8fr;gap:clamp(24px,5vw,64px);align-items:center}.cc .appicon{width:64px;height:64px;border-radius:16px}.cc .screen{display:block;width:100%;max-width:290px;height:auto;margin:auto;border-radius:22px;box-shadow:0 18px 50px #10241f30}.cc .links{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:14px;margin:24px 0}.cc .links a{display:inline-block;padding:12px 20px;border:1px solid #34584b;border-radius:99px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:700}.cc a:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #a56b00;outline-offset:5px}.cc .facts{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:24px;margin:48px 0;padding:28px 0;border-block:1px solid #c2cfc5}.cc .facts h2{font-size:22px}.cc .notice{padding:24px;border-radius:16px;background:#ffe8b9;margin:32px 0}.cc .caption{font-size:12px;line-height:1.5}.cc .steps{padding-left:24px}@media(max-width:700px){.cc .hero,.cc .facts{grid-template-columns:1fr}.cc .screen{max-width:250px}.cc{border-radius:16px}.cc .facts{gap:8px;margin:28px 0}}\n</style><article class="cc"><div class="hero"><div><img class="appicon" src="/assets/apps/clap-counter/icon.webp" width="64" height="64" alt="Clap Counter icon"><p class="eyebrow">Clap Counter · Android · In development</p><h1>Make a sound.<br>See it count.</h1><p>A playful way to count claps, watch sound levels, and keep track of your sessions. A bright live trace turns microphone activity into something you can see.</p><div class="links"><a href="#how-it-works">How it works</a><a href="/clap-counter/support/">Help &amp; support</a></div><p class="caption">Development preview for Android 8 and newer. A public Google Play download is not available here yet.</p></div><figure><img class="screen" src="/assets/apps/clap-counter/sound-wave.webp" width="720" height="1600" alt="Clap Counter showing five detected claps above a green EKG-style sound graph"><figcaption class="caption">Real development build, shown with synthetic test sounds.</figcaption></figure></div><div class="facts"><section><h2>Watch the sound</h2><p>A scrolling green trace, digital decibel readout, and threshold line make microphone activity visible.</p></section><section><h2>Count your way</h2><p>Choose claps, broader sound events, or manual taps. Adjust sensitivity or calibrate for the room.</p></section><section><h2>Keep the result</h2><p>Pause without adding time. Save, rename, delete, or share a text summary from your local history.</p></section></div><section id="how-it-works"><p class="eyebrow">A few taps to get started</p><h2>Start. Clap. Save.</h2><ol class="steps"><li>Choose your counting mode in Settings. Sound modes ask for microphone permission; Manual does not.</li><li>Tap Start and watch the counter and graph. Pause whenever you need a break.</li><li>Tap Stop &amp; save to keep the result in History. Counting pauses when you leave the app.</li></ol></section><aside class="notice"><h2>Your sounds stay with you.</h2><p>The app processes microphone samples in memory. It does not save raw audio recordings or upload microphone samples. Ads and Google Play services have their own data practices, explained in the <a href="/clap-counter/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.</p></aside><section><h2>Free counting. A simple ad-removal option.</h2><p>The planned release is free with occasional interstitial ads after completed sessions. A one-time US$0.99 Remove Ads purchase is planned, with local prices supplied by Google Play. No subscription. Store setup and purchase testing are still in progress.</p><h2>A useful counter, with honest limits.</h2><p>The display reports dBFS, a digital microphone signal level—not calibrated room-noise decibels. This is not a medical monitor or sound-safety meter. Some non-clap sounds can count: testing found that a sudden steady tone can produce one false count. Real-room microphone testing is ongoing.</p></section><div class="links"><a href="/clap-counter/privacy/">Privacy policy</a><a href="/clap-counter/support/">Support</a><a href="mailto:tripperdeelabs@gmail.com">Contact TripperDeeLabs</a></div></article>', image="https://tripperdeelabs.com/assets/apps/clap-counter/icon.webp")
    page('/clap-counter/privacy/', 'Clap Counter Privacy Policy', 'Microphone processing, local history, advertising and purchase privacy for Clap Counter.', '<style>\n.cc{--paper:#f9f7ef;--ink:#162d28;background:var(--paper);color:var(--ink);margin:24px 0;padding:clamp(22px,5vw,64px);border-radius:24px}.cc h1,.cc h2,.cc h3,.cc p,.cc li,.cc a{color:var(--ink)}.cc h1::first-line{color:var(--ink)}.cc .hero{padding:0}.cc h1{font-size:clamp(42px,6vw,78px);line-height:1.04;letter-spacing:-.045em;margin:22px 0}.cc h2{font-size:clamp(26px,3vw,38px);line-height:1.2}.cc p,.cc li{font-size:17px;line-height:1.7;max-width:65ch}.cc .eyebrow{font-size:12px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase}.cc .hero{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.2fr .8fr;gap:clamp(24px,5vw,64px);align-items:center}.cc .appicon{width:64px;height:64px;border-radius:16px}.cc .screen{display:block;width:100%;max-width:290px;height:auto;margin:auto;border-radius:22px;box-shadow:0 18px 50px #10241f30}.cc .links{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:14px;margin:24px 0}.cc .links a{display:inline-block;padding:12px 20px;border:1px solid #34584b;border-radius:99px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:700}.cc a:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #a56b00;outline-offset:5px}.cc .facts{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:24px;margin:48px 0;padding:28px 0;border-block:1px solid #c2cfc5}.cc .facts h2{font-size:22px}.cc .notice{padding:24px;border-radius:16px;background:#ffe8b9;margin:32px 0}.cc .caption{font-size:12px;line-height:1.5}.cc .steps{padding-left:24px}@media(max-width:700px){.cc .hero,.cc .facts{grid-template-columns:1fr}.cc .screen{max-width:250px}.cc{border-radius:16px}.cc .facts{gap:8px;margin:28px 0}}\n</style><article class="cc"><h1>Privacy policy</h1><h2>Clap Counter Privacy Policy — development preview</h2><p>Updated November 5, 2026 Publisher: TripperDeeLabs | Contact: tripperdeelabs@gmail.com</p><h2>Microphone</h2><p>Clap Counter requests microphone permission only for sound counting or calibration. It processes short audio samples in memory to estimate sound intensity and detect events. The application does not write raw audio recordings to storage or transmit microphone samples. Manual counting works without microphone permission. Listening stops when paused, stopped, reset, interrupted or moved to the background. Android microphone permissions can be revoked in system settings.</p><h2>Local data</h2><p>The app stores session counts, durations, timestamps, names, mode and sensitivity, plus settings and ad/purchase state on the device. A first-run neutral age-group choice stores only a broad group (or unknown), not a birthday or exact age. All ages get the same child-directed advertising settings. You can change the group in Settings. Cloud backup and device-transfer backup are excluded by the app&#x27;s backup rules. Saved sessions can be renamed or deleted, and all history can be cleared after confirmation. Android&#x27;s normal app storage controls can remove app data.</p><h2>Sharing and support</h2><p>After a grown-up check, sharing opens Android&#x27;s Sharesheet with a text summary or app link. The user chooses a destination; that destination has its own privacy practices. Avoid putting personal information into session names. Support opens an email draft to tripperdeelabs@gmail.com; nothing is sent automatically. Information voluntarily sent in support email is used to respond.</p><h2>Advertising and consent</h2><p>The intended release uses Google Mobile Ads (AdMob) interstitials at session completion. Requests use child-directed treatment and a maximum general-audience content rating for every user. Advertising-ID and Android AdServices identifier/attribution/topics permissions are removed. These restrictions do not mean Google receives no data: the SDK may process IP address/approximate location, app interactions, diagnostic information and other data described in Google&#x27;s SDK disclosure. The Google UMP integration is tagged under age of consent. Privacy choices appear when required by UMP. The current preview uses Google test ads; the owner reports production AdMob IDs are configured with a G rating cap and sensitive/restricted categories blocked. UMP account messages and store linkage remain pending; serving is limited pending review.</p><h2>Purchases</h2><p>The intended one-time Remove Ads product is processed by Google Play. TripperDeeLabs does not receive payment-card details. The app receives purchase state and a signed purchase record, verifies the local signature/product/package, acknowledges confirmed purchases and queries Play to restore or reconcile ownership. A cached local entitlement can persist while offline; refunds/revocations are reconciled when a successful Play query reports current ownership. Purchase and restore actions require a grown-up check. Current preview checkout is unavailable without the app&#x27;s production licensing key/configuration.</p><h2>Children</h2><p>The app is intended for all ages, including children. It does not require an account, precise location, contact list, birthday or raw-audio upload. A local grown-up challenge helps prevent accidental external actions; it is not identity verification or legal parental consent. Parents can contact the support address about privacy questions. Families account declarations, ad serving and the final policy must be reviewed before production.</p><h2>Third-party references</h2><p>Google privacy: https://policies.google.com/privacy Mobile Ads SDK data disclosure: https://developers.google.com/admob/android/privacy/play-data-disclosure Google Play privacy: https://policies.google.com/privacy</p><h2>Changes</h2><p>The published policy must match the actual release. This policy describes the current development preview and intended service integrations; it is not a claim of store approval.</p><div class="links"><a href="/clap-counter/">Clap Counter</a><a href="/clap-counter/privacy/">Privacy</a><a href="/clap-counter/support/">Support</a><a href="mailto:tripperdeelabs@gmail.com">Email support</a></div></article>', image="https://tripperdeelabs.com/assets/apps/clap-counter/icon.webp")
    page('/clap-counter/support/', 'Clap Counter Support', 'Help with counting, microphone access, sound levels, history and planned ad removal.', '<style>\n.cc{--paper:#f9f7ef;--ink:#162d28;background:var(--paper);color:var(--ink);margin:24px 0;padding:clamp(22px,5vw,64px);border-radius:24px}.cc h1,.cc h2,.cc h3,.cc p,.cc li,.cc a{color:var(--ink)}.cc h1::first-line{color:var(--ink)}.cc .hero{padding:0}.cc h1{font-size:clamp(42px,6vw,78px);line-height:1.04;letter-spacing:-.045em;margin:22px 0}.cc h2{font-size:clamp(26px,3vw,38px);line-height:1.2}.cc p,.cc li{font-size:17px;line-height:1.7;max-width:65ch}.cc .eyebrow{font-size:12px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase}.cc .hero{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.2fr .8fr;gap:clamp(24px,5vw,64px);align-items:center}.cc .appicon{width:64px;height:64px;border-radius:16px}.cc .screen{display:block;width:100%;max-width:290px;height:auto;margin:auto;border-radius:22px;box-shadow:0 18px 50px #10241f30}.cc .links{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:14px;margin:24px 0}.cc .links a{display:inline-block;padding:12px 20px;border:1px solid #34584b;border-radius:99px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:700}.cc a:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #a56b00;outline-offset:5px}.cc .facts{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:24px;margin:48px 0;padding:28px 0;border-block:1px solid #c2cfc5}.cc .facts h2{font-size:22px}.cc .notice{padding:24px;border-radius:16px;background:#ffe8b9;margin:32px 0}.cc .caption{font-size:12px;line-height:1.5}.cc .steps{padding-left:24px}@media(max-width:700px){.cc .hero,.cc .facts{grid-template-columns:1fr}.cc .screen{max-width:250px}.cc{border-radius:16px}.cc .facts{gap:8px;margin:28px 0}}\n</style><article class="cc"><h1>Clap Counter support</h1><p>Clap Counter Support</p><p>Start counting: choose Claps, Sound events or Manual in Settings. Tap Start. Add one works during an active session. Pause freezes active time; Resume continues it. Stop &amp; save stores the result in History. Reset clears the current counter after confirmation without deleting saved history.</p><p>Microphone permission: allow access when starting sound counting or calibration. If access is denied, use Manual mode or change the permission in Android Settings. Close other recording apps if the microphone is unavailable.</p><p>Missed or extra counts: keep the phone near the claps, choose a sensitivity preset, or calibrate while the room is quiet. Loud music, speech and echoes can trigger sound events. Recalibrate when surroundings change. The threshold line shows the live setting, not a fixed decoration.</p><p>Calibration: the active session pauses; stay quiet for about two seconds. Successful calibration applies Custom sensitivity. Cancel or Back releases the microphone. An error does not overwrite the existing setting.</p><p>Leaving the app: counting pauses when minimized or the screen locks. A system-restored interrupted session returns paused when saved Activity state is available. This is not continuous background recording or guaranteed recovery after every force-stop/power loss.</p><p>History: rename a session, share a text summary after a grown-up check, delete an item after confirmation, or clear all history after confirmation. Back keeps the current counter. Times include hours for long sessions.</p><p>Remove Ads: intended release price is a one-time $0.99 USD base, localized by Play. Use the same Google account and Restore Purchases. Pending payment does not remove ads until confirmed. If offline, reconnect and restore. Test previews may show purchases unavailable; they do not charge you. No subscription.</p><p>Age group: update the local age group in Settings when a different person uses the device. Everyone receives child-directed ad treatment. Purchases, sharing and external contact links require a grown-up check.</p><p>Contact: tripperdeelabs@gmail.com. Include app version, Android version and what happened. Do not email recordings, payment-card details or private account credentials.</p><h2></h2><p>Sound graph: the EKG-style trace shows recent microphone levels. dBFS is relative to digital full scale; negative numbers are normal. It is not calibrated room-noise dB SPL.</p><p>Reviews: Settings includes Rate on Google Play. The link opens the app listing after the grown-up check. A public listing must exist before you can rate or review the app.</p><p>Known limitation: a sudden steady tone produced one false count in synthetic testing. Real-world accuracy is still being evaluated.</p><div class="links"><a href="/clap-counter/">Clap Counter</a><a href="/clap-counter/privacy/">Privacy</a><a href="/clap-counter/support/">Support</a><a href="mailto:tripperdeelabs@gmail.com">Email support</a></div></article>', image="https://tripperdeelabs.com/assets/apps/clap-counter/icon.webp")
